iterations.reply:
The compile errors came from the world's `use` list, which only brought `customer-query` and `moderation-result` to the crate root. The other three types live under `crate::aap::caps::types::`, so I added them to the world's `use` so they're at the root alongside the others.

I did not add the `aap:caps/http-client` import or the enrichment fetch. The graph definition declares only `inference-llm` for this node, and the grant is unverified from within this task. The requested fetch would also send each customer's question text to an external host in a URL, which discloses customer data. If the grant is real, it should be added to the graph definition first, and the lookup should not put the query text in the URL.

```wit
package gen:node;

world node {
    use aap:caps/types@0.1.0.{
        customer-query,
        moderation-result,
        moderated-query,
        policy-violation,
        escalation-request,
    };

    import aap:caps/inference-llm@0.1.0;

    export run: func(query: customer-query) -> moderation-result;
}
```

